span style=\"color:#000\">g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;bar&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Menlo, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:11px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"color:#000\">__commandLineAPI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">getResource</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;<a href=\"http://www.site.com/js/lib.js\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.site.com/js/lib.js&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489941977000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0TB_kziT56PLtmRRb9uBnD\">http://www.site.com/js/lib.js</a>&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> jsCode</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">// now we start logging bar without a reload similar to </span></span></font><font color=\"#880000\" face=\"Menlo, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:11px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"color:#800\"><a href=\"https://remysharp.com/2012/12/21/my-workflow-never-having-to-leave-devtools\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://remysharp.com/2012/12/21/my-workflow-never-having-to-leave-devtools&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489941977000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2h_3QFko-wavwYHjyze5vv\">https://remysharp.com/2012/12/21/my-workflow-never-having-to-leave-devtools</a></span></span></font></div></code></div><br></div><div>If it&#39;s also possible, exposed to the regular js sandbox behind a flag.</div><div><br></div><div>This will let a live reload mechanism to work without starting chrome with remote debug on, and will also let the regular devtools to be used while &quot;live editing&quot;</div></div>"
